      "mergeID": "68f10178b9b15e600629a0fe",
      "mergedPostDetails": "I've been experiencing this bug on/off over the last year or more. You can still hear them interacting with other players, which is usually what gives it away since they're completely frozen in place and not animating at all. The number of affected users seems random each time as well. I've had some lobbies where 8 or more players are scattered around the map frozen in place. Also seems to be most common with game worlds, but that may be because that's mostly all I play (but I never see this bug in Furry Hideout, for instance).\n\nThe bug is easily fixed if you just find the user in question, select them, and show their avatar. You can even re-hide it, it just needs to try to update the avatar at all and they'll immediately be fixed.\n\nExample video showing off the bug (and fixing it): https://youtu.be/RLL0fWV9OcI\n\nRepro steps:\n\n1. Open VRChat\n\n2. Update your shield settings to disable avatars and only show robots for MOST if not all players\n\n3. Join an instance and look for players that aren't moving or animating, but are still talking as if they're actively playing the game.\n\n4. Toggle their avatar visibility to fix the issue, which confirms that was the bug.\n\nP.S. only play on PC, no clue if this happens for any other platform.",
